  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Quiet weather.\n\nYou can expect the Nor'easter off the mid-Atlantic coast to\nbring some gusty winds today and Sunday to portions of our area\nmainly in the 15-25 mph range. Some mid and high clouds could\nsurge southward at times but overall mostly clear skies\nexpected. Should be a good sunset/evening to watch the Harvest\nmoon rise.\n\nThrough the middle of next week, 5h heights build and\ntemperatures will start rising above normal, though with drier\nairmass, low temps may be closer to normal. \n\nUpper ridge breaks down next weekend as a trough pushes into the\nMidwest. Should see moisture increasing by Saturday with shower\nchances returning.",
